  "full_response": "**Developer Onboarding Document: API Keys and Access Tokens**\n\nWelcome to the team! This document is designed to help you get started with accessing the necessary API keys and access tokens. Please follow the instructions carefully and replace the sample values with your actual credentials.\n\n### 1. GitHub Access Token\n**Purpose:** Access GitHub repositories and APIs for managing code and deploying updates.\n\n- **How to Obtain:**\n  1. Go to [GitHub Settings](https://github.com/settings/tokens).\n  2. Click on \"Generate new token\".\n  3. Select appropriate scopes for your tasks (e.g., repo, admin:org).\n  4. Click \"Generate token\" and copy it.\n\n- **Sample Value:** `ghp_AbCdEf1234567890ABCDEF12ghijklmn`\n- **Environment Variable:** Set as `GITHUB_TOKEN` in your local environment or CI/CD pipelines.\n\n### 2. AWS Access Key and Secret Key\n**Purpose:** Access and manage Amazon Web Services for cloud resources, including EC2 instances, S3 buckets, and RDS databases.\n\n- **How to Obtain:**\n  1. Sign in to the [AWS Management Console](https://aws.amazon.com/console/).\n  2. Navigate to \"Security Credentials\".\n  3. Create a new access key under \"Access keys (access key ID and secret access key)\".\n\n- **Sample Values:**\n  - Access Key ID: `AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE`\n  - Secret Access Key: `wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY`\n- **Environment Variables:**\n  - `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`\n  - `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`\n\n### 3. Slack API Token\n**Purpose:** Interact with Slack for notifications, messages, and integrating your applications with Slack workflows.\n\n- **How to Obtain:**\n  1. Go to [Your Apps](https://api.slack.com/apps) on Slack API.\n  2. Create a new app or connect to an existing app.\n  3. Under \"OAuth & Permissions\", install the app to your workspace to get an access token.\n\n- **Sample Value:** `xoxb-1234567890-0987654321-nMzYzZMYvqQjVjVZJZjUIzx`\n- **Environment Variable:** Set as `SLACK_API_TOKEN`.\n\n### 4. Stripe",
